Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:45:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1155/1198] HERESY 1167: the polish: the Score's tools as icons
 with A4 and the sheet's side, a Direct take's score from its sound, the
 Creator's two frames by width, the tall bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 05.10.2026, «микро моменты по шлифовке интерфейса»:
· the cheat-sheet's lead paragraph runs the sheet's width («убери ручные переносы строк»);
· the Score's tools are icons where the icon says it (print, portrait, landscape, markers, edit and re-render, full screen;
  «Full Screen надпись убрать, но иконку чётче»), MIDI keeps its word; the paper is US Letter or A4, the sheet upright or on
  its side, both remembered (yue2.paper, yue2.paperSide) and given to print as @page;
· a Direct take has no score of its own: the Score panel writes it from the take's sound in place (the lab's /score,
  SheetSage2), no Cover detour («генерации ABC из самого трека, чтобы не прогонять его через Cover»);
· from 1400 px the line between the form and the take is dragged: the form 55 to 70 % of the width; below 55 it snaps to
  40, the takes take 60 % and the form stands in one column; double-click or Home for the default, arrows move it
  (yue2.kWidth);
· the bar is 40 pt taller (105 px, from 1660 px) while the page stands at its top, the logo with it, and its usual 52 px
  once a room scrolls 60 px. The height itself is the animated value (@property --bar-h), so the rooms under the bar, the
  sticky bands and the logo move with it: animated alone, for 0.22 s the page overflowed (a scrollbar came and went and
  the columns lost 9 px). 60 px is more than the 53 the bar loses, so where the whole page scrolls (Engine) the browser's
  scroll anchoring cannot land under 4 px and grow it again.
The console test measures the bar instead of 52 px and waits for it to settle; 18 new keys in the six catalogs.
cdp-console 330/0/7, check-i18n 14/0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
